# hyper-ui

`@malini/hyper-ui` is the design system. Import the folder module `$hyper-ui/components/<kebab-name>`, never a `.svelte` path inside it. Icons are `<Icon name="…" />` from `$hyper-ui/icons`.

Rules:

- Use a hyper-ui component before writing a control. Buttons, form controls, overlays, and modals exist.
- Design tokens only. No literal colors. No legacy tokens. No opacity on semantic tokens.
- Use the surface/border token pair that matches. `border` tokens are not backgrounds.
- Foreground tokens are for text and icons. A non-text use is a rule violation.
- No native `title` attribute. Use the hyper-ui tooltip.
- No bespoke overlay or modal implementations. Use the hyper-ui primitives.
- No motion while the window is hidden, or it all plays at once on return. A transition reads `motionOff()` from `$hyper-ui/motion/motion-off` (or `motionMs()` in the chat) where it starts.
- Every rule runs at `error`, enforced by `@malini/desktop/*` in `packages/eslint-plugin-hyper-ui`.
- Do not edit a `*.generated.ts` file. Edit its source and rerun the generator.

Style cost (ADR 0199, not linted):

- No daisyUI component classes. The app loads daisyUI with `include: properties`, for its theme colors only.
- No global rule that ends in `*`, or in a `:where()` or `:is()` with no class, tag or id. Chrome tries it on every element in every style pass.
- A list that grows with history, such as the archived workstreams, renders only the rows in view.
